    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thats a fair point about social unrest. but i feel like we always hear about \"economic stability\" as a reason to delay, yet we rarely hear any actual quantitative proof that we can't just innovate our way through the costs. isn't it more accurate to say that the economic argument is just a political tool used to protect legacy industries rather than a legitimate barrier to survival?",
