      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is certainly a common criticism that the economic argument acts as a convenient shield for vested interests slowing down change. While some delays can be attributed to lobbying, the concept of economic viability remains a genuine concern regarding energy accessibility for all citizens. Developing the necessary clean energy infrastructure at a pace that meets current demand is a monumental technical challenge, not just a matter of capital. Ultimately, overcoming this requires massive public investment and coordinated policy that accepts short-term structural costs for long-term systemic resilience.",
      "source": "target",
